Proposal: extend the static AST binding census to constant-false `while` loops
Target: tools/check-revision-binding.py, `shared()`/`visit()` (baseline lines 293-297)
Impact: per-tool `shared` flag (line 908-909) and `consolidated_tools` (line 918-919)

--- a/tools/check-revision-binding.py
+++ b/tools/check-revision-binding.py
@@ -293,7 +293,7 @@ def shared(source):
     def visit(node):
-        if isinstance(node, ast.If) and isinstance(node.test, ast.Constant):
+        if isinstance(node, (ast.If, ast.While)) and isinstance(node.test, ast.Constant):
             body = node.body if node.test.value else node.orelse
             for child in body:
                 visit(child)
```

Semantics note: for a `while` whose test is a literal constant, the branch
selection is identical to `if`: body executes iff the constant is truthy, and
the orelse executes iff it is falsy (the `else` of a `while False:` runs once —
Python executes it on normal termination, which a false condition is).  The
same branch formula is therefore correct for both node kinds; the fixture matrix
locks this with `live-while-else-live-bind` → (True, 0) and
`live-while-true-body-bind` → (True, 0), which pass on both baseline and patched
census.

Recommended selftest additions (same file, `selftest()` `check(...)` block near
lines 1286-1292):

    check("dead-while-literal-bind", shared("while False:\n    import _revision\n"
                                              "    _revision.bind(r,v)\n"), (False, 0))
    check("live-while-else-bind", shared("while False:\n    pass\nelse:\n"
                                          "    import _revision\n"
                                          "    _revision.bind(r,v)\n"), (True, 0))
